* ============================================================================
* rel_name_ambiguity_regression.dts
*
* AIF-120 I1.3a. ONE RESOLVER, AND AN AMBIGUOUS NAME NOW SAYS SO.
*
* WHAT WAS WRONG
*   Two functions answered "which open area is called X" and they did not
*   agree. find_open_area_by_name_ci (workarea_util.cpp, 21 call sites)
*   returned the FIRST match -- the lowest engine slot. build_area_by_up_name
*   (set_relations.cpp, the recursive REL LIST tree builder) built its own map
*   with an unconditional `out[key] = a`, which makes it the LAST match -- the
*   highest slot. Same question, two answers, and neither said which area it
*   had picked.
*
*   R112 sec 3 measured the reach: twelve basenames -- students, teachers,
*   classes, enroll, courses, dept, majors, rooms, stud_maj, tassign, terms,
*   building -- exist in all three of dbf/x64, dbf/x32 and dbf/vfp. That is
*   the MCC demo corpus, not a corner case. And it needs no second workspace:
*   USE guards duplicates by PATH only, and USE ... ALIAS sets the logical name
*   with no uniqueness check at all, which is how this script builds its
*   fixture in one workspace.
*
* WHAT THIS SPEC CAN AND CANNOT SEE, stated rather than implied.
*   The divergence itself is NOT field-observable. build_area_by_up_name's map
*   fed record counts that get PRINTED; it never moved a cursor. So no marker
*   here goes red on the old build, and this spec is not a discriminator for
*   the consolidation -- the compiler is, because the function is gone and
*   cannot be called. Saying so is the point: a spec that cannot fail on the
*   defect it is named after is the false green this house keeps finding.
*
*   What the markers DO pin is the ruled CHOICE. R112 sec 6a ruled first-wins
*   plus an instrumented warning as the migration step toward requiring
*   qualification. N_T1/N_T2 assert that choice by field value, so the day the
*   policy flips to a hard refusal these two lines move -- the flip becomes a
*   red marker and its own ruling, which is what "time-boxed by measurement"
*   has to mean if it means anything.
*
* N_T2 IS THE DISCRIMINATOR FOR DIRECTION. NAMLO and NAMHI are both open under
*   the logical name NAMDUP, in areas 1 and 2. The parent moves; exactly one
*   child follows. A green N_T2 says the HIGHER slot stayed put -- if anyone
*   ever "fixes" ambiguity by making the last match win, N_T2 reds and N_T1
*   reds with it.
*
* THE LEDGER IS TRANSCRIPT EVIDENCE, read by a human or a gate, not by a
*   marker. WORKSPACE REGISTRY prints `name ambiguity : N resolution(s)` and
*   one row per distinct (name, call site). The NAME-AMBIGUITY-LEDGER block
*   MUST contain a non-zero count and a NAMDUP row; the same field printed as
*   0 in a run that opened no duplicates is the measured zero R112 makes the
*   gate for turning first-wins into a refusal.
*
* Self-bootstrapping NAMPAR/NAMLO/NAMHI in SANDBOX, self-erasing.
*   Standalone:  DO rel_name_ambiguity_regression
*   Regression:  REGRESSION RUN NAME_AMBIG
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX

FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-BEGIN"

REL CLEAR ALL
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE nampar CONFIRM
ERASE namlo CONFIRM
ERASE namhi CONFIRM

* --- fixture: one parent, two children that will share a name --------------
SELECT 0
CREATE X64 NAMPAR (PK C(4))
APPEND
REPLACE PK WITH "A"
APPEND
REPLACE PK WITH "B"

SELECT 1
CREATE X64 NAMLO (CK C(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "A"
REPLACE MARK WITH "LOW_A"
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "B"
REPLACE MARK WITH "LOW_B"

SELECT 2
CREATE X64 NAMHI (CK C(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "A"
REPLACE MARK WITH "HIGH_A"
APPEND
REPLACE CK WITH "B"
REPLACE MARK WITH "HIGH_B"

WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL

* --- the collision, built in ONE workspace with no second root -------------
* USE ... ALIAS is a RENAME (R112 sec 1: alias= and ALIAS both assign
* _logical_name) and it performs NO uniqueness check. Two areas, one name.
SELECT 0
USE nampar
SELECT 1
USE namlo ALIAS NAMDUP
SELECT 2
USE namhi ALIAS NAMDUP

SELECT 1
GO TOP
? "N_G0_low_area_holds_low:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "LOW_A")
SELECT 2
GO TOP
? "N_G1_high_area_holds_high:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "HIGH_A")

* --- the ambiguous resolution, announced -----------------------------------
* REL ADD resolves the child name NAMDUP. Two areas match. The block below
* MUST contain a NAME: line naming both candidates and the area chosen.
SELECT 0
GO TOP
FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-ANNOUNCE-BEGIN"
REL ADD NAMPAR NAMDUP ON PK TO CK
FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-ANNOUNCE-END"

* --- move the parent; exactly one child follows ----------------------------
SKIP

SELECT 1
? "N_T1_lowest_slot_followed_the_parent:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "LOW_B")
SELECT 2
? "N_T2_higher_slot_did_not_follow:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "HIGH_A")

* --- the instrument, read ---------------------------------------------------
FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-LEDGER-BEGIN"
WORKSPACE REGISTRY
FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-LEDGER-END"

* --- teardown --------------------------------------------------------------
REL CLEAR ALL
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE nampar CONFIRM
ERASE namlo CONFIRM
ERASE namhi CONFIRM

FORMULA "NAME-AMBIGUITY-END"
